Restore the web client's last active workspace after a restart

After a workspace restart the tile lands on Landing - "Select a workspace from
the sidebar to begin" - even though the sidebar lists every worktree.

Upstream's paired-client session read already restores this from
`ui.lastActiveRepoId` and `ui.lastActiveWorktreeId`, but nothing anywhere writes
those two fields: the producer was never implemented, on desktop or on web. It
belongs in `usePersistedUIWriter`, the shared renderer writer that already
mirrors store fields into the durable UI file, beside its `activeView` effect -
a dedicated effect for a value that changes on every switch, deliberately kept
off the 150 ms multi-MB durable-state save (#9002). Everything downstream of
`window.api.ui.set` already exists end to end: the web adapter writes
localStorage first and forwards over `ui.set`, and `lastActive*` is not a
pairing-local field, so it crosses the pairing boundary both ways. Writing it in
the shared renderer fills the gap on desktop and web at once.

`getStoredWorkspaceSession` then falls back to the browser's own sanitized copy
when the host pointer is absent, for a client paired before the pointer was ever
recorded. That fallback also does the carry-forward work: `session.patch` merges
onto `getStoredWorkspaceSession`, so with a null merge base a patch carrying only
`activeWorktreeId` would erase the repo pointer beside it.

To test, open a worktree in the tile, restart the workspace, and reload: that
worktree should be active. Switch worktrees within a repo and reload again - the
repo must not be lost. Repeat in a browser with cleared storage. Red with this
patch popped: `use-persisted-ui-writer-active-workspace.test.ts` - three of four -
and `web-workspace-restore.test.ts` - two of four. Both files are load-bearing.
